+### 4.2 Forced cyclic action on one nonzero packet
+
+For every group the bottom denominator increment is `A_1=2` and
+`Q_1=3=1*2+1`.  The stabilizer acts by `pi -> -pi`; the star roots split as
+the fixed root `{0}` and the pair `{-1,+1}`.
+
+At level two the data are:
+
+| group | `A_2` | `Q_2=V_3 d_2/d_3=u` | division | selected `V_2=1` branch |
+|---|---:|---:|---|---|
+| A | 18 | 25 | `25=1*18+7` | (10), nonzero root |
+| B | 13 | 30 | `30=2*13+4` | (10), nonzero root |
+| C | 17 | 28 | `28=1*17+11` | (10), nonzero root |
+
+Moh's automorphism mechanism, transcribed and explained at
+`census-rebase-opus5-20260902.md:137-149`, says a selected nonzero factor is
+accompanied by its full orbit of `A_2` distinct conjugate factors.  Let
+`zeta` be a primitive `R_delta`-th root, let
+`r_i=R_delta*delta_i`, choose a nonzero centre coefficient `b`, and write the
+shared ancestor prefix as `w_<delta2`.  The forced leading packet is
+
+```text
+tau_(j,c)(z)
+ = w_<delta2(zeta^j z)
+   + b zeta^(r_2 j) z^r_2
+   + c zeta^(r_1 j) z^r_1
+   + higher,
+
+j mod A_2,    c in {-1,0,+1}.
+```
+
+The three substitutions are:
+
+```text
+A: R=36, A_2=18, (r_2,r_1)=(14,21)
+B: R=26, A_2=13, (r_2,r_1)=(4,11)
+C: R=34, A_2=17, (r_2,r_1)=(8,19).
+```
+
+After `A_2` applications of `z -> zeta z`, the centre returns and
+`zeta^(r_1 A_2)=-1`, so `c` changes to `-c`.  Hence this marked packet has two
+orbits on **leaves**, of sizes `A_2` for `c=0` and `2A_2` for the combined
+nonzero leaves.  These leaf orbits must not be confused with the one orbit on
+bottom discs.
+
+At every later exponent `r`, honest shared coefficients must transform by
+
+```text
+u_(j+1,c,r) = zeta^r u_(j,c,r),
+```
+
+with the wrap sending `c` to `-c`.  Giving every branch an independent tail,
+or merely giving conjugate tails the same symbol without the character
+factor, is not this decoration.
+
+### 4.3 UNI and the requested “coarsest split”
+
+The arithmetic identity `N=k V_2 q`, together with `kV_2<=u`, yields the nine
+formal choices in the charge.  It is a capacity/integrality computation, not
+an orbit construction or attainment theorem.
