+```
+
+Only those frozen copies and the new files in
+`box/d105rank-drivers-20260903/` were read.  In particular, no other
+`ideation-20260903T1015Z-*` file and no other running lane report was read.
+
+The frozen census lists the three rows at
+`census-rebase-opus5-20260902.md:474-487`; the compact charged listing
+independently gives the same rows at `survivors-D48-120.txt:5-8`.  The blind
+count is at `ideation-20260903T1015Z-gpt55.md:117-181`.  The framework's
+information obstruction and exact decorated-input contract are at
+`global-interpolation-sol56-20260902.md:461-514`.
+
+## 2. What the sealed framework actually requires
+
+Put `t=x^-1` and choose a common field `C((z))` with `x=z^-R`.  For a requested
+last exponent `Q`, the report's decorated skeleton is
+
+```text
+D_Q = (bare Moh tuple,
+       rooted cluster tree on n labelled leaves,
+       cyclic Galois action and orbit/stabilizer data,
+       truncated Puiseux template tau_i(z) for every leaf,
+       declarations identifying shared tame coefficients,
+       Q and a sufficient valuation guard).
+```
+
+This contract is substantive, not serialization overhead.  If
+`D_i=product_(j!=i)(tau_i-tau_j)`, then every entry of `D_i^-1`, every time
+value, and every moment sees contacts with all other 104 roots.  A missing
+outer leaf can change a denominator leader, the first retained exponent, a
+residue, a moment coefficient, and the rank.
+
+For a complete decoration the intrinsic unknown count is
+
+```text
+U(Q) = h + u_0 + |Z_Q|,                                    (4.13)
+```
+
+where `h` is the number of branch orbits, `u_0` is the number of
+unspecialized leading/star parameters after gauges, and `Z_Q` is the set of
+independent tame symbols that can reach the equations through the complete
+inverse/integration guard.  None of `h`, `u_0`, or `Z_Q` follows from `k`.
+In particular, “one orbit of bottom discs” does not by itself give the number
+of orbits on the 105 leaves, and two local kernel coordinates per displayed
+disc are not formula (4.13).
+
+Likewise the intrinsic equation count is
+
+```text
+C(Q) = C_res + C_deg(Q) + C_poly(Q),                        (4.11)
+C_res = h.
+```
+
+Its `C_deg` summands require the initial exponents of the 35 moment identities;
+its `C_poly` summands require the initial exponents of the surviving
+coefficients.  Those exponents are absent here.  The normalized shortcut
+`C=h+35+105K` applies only after one has proved the stationary invariant
+support `t^0,...,t^K`; it cannot be used to invent that support.
+
+### 2.1 Implementation audit of `globalinterp.py`
+
+The sealed implementation is valuable for custody of the exact finite
+straight-line lift and for the controls, but it cannot silently repair the
+missing decoration.
+
+* It requires exactly `n` branch objects, yet it has no JSON object for a
+  rooted tree, cyclic permutation, stabilizer, or sharing equivalence
+  relation.  It infers pairwise contacts and trusts an orbit's
+  `verified=true` flag.
+* A direct probe changed its passing two-branch example from the equivariant
+  pair `I z^-1,-I z^-1` to `I z^-1,-2I z^-1`, retained `verified=true`, and
+  the driver accepted it, reduced NO-RESIDUE to one effective row, and reused
+  one integration constant.  A D=105 wrapper must therefore validate
+  covariance before invoking the sealed orbit shortcut.
+* Its reported unknown count includes product, inverse, power, time, and
+  polynomial-coefficient auxiliaries.  It is not (4.13).  Its reported rank
+  is the ambient Jacobian rank of that lifted system, not the rank of the
+  descended intrinsic moment map at a solution.
+* It orbit-reduces only the metadata count for NO-RESIDUE; it does not project
+  all equations to the trivial character before ranking.
+* It lists inequations but has no saturation or ideal-emptiness routine.
+* Missing exact coefficients are interpreted as zero; `tail_from` creates an
+  unlimited free tail.  There is no independent finite “last supplied
+  coefficient” with which to certify a genuinely truncated algebraic input.
+
+The unsymmetrized lift is also the wrong computational representation for
+this target.  At one coefficient it already has `105*104=10,920` prefix
+products, 105 inverses, and at least `105*69=7,245` nontrivial power nodes.
+For the driver's illustrative `tau_i=(i+1)z^-1`, `m=70`, `qmax=0` recurrence,
+the power count is 514,395 before time and evaluation equations.  This is why
+the next valid implementation should form the 35 character-projected moments
+directly.  The present lane was stopped for missing mathematical input before
+spending the 30-minute/6-GB allowance on a matrix for a synthetic completion.
+
+## 3. Exact arithmetic forced by the three groups
+
+For all groups, `n=105`, `m=70`, `K=35`, `(d,e)=(2,3)`, `V_2=1`, and
+`M_1=-70`, `M_3=103`.  Applying the frozen implementation of Moh's radius
+formula gives:
+
+| group | `M_2,V_3,u,q` | `d_1,d_2,d_3,d_4` | `delta_1,delta_2,delta_3` | minimal `R_delta` | `(R delta_3,R delta_2,R delta_1)` | `J_2/R = delta_1-delta_2` | minimal `J_2` |
+|---|---|---|---|---:|---|---|---:|
+| A | `28,5,25,1/2` | `105,35,7,1` | `7/12,7/18,-1` | 36 | `(-36,14,21)` | `7/36` | 7 |
+| B | `28,6,30,9/13` | `105,35,7,1` | `11/26,2/13,-1` | 26 | `(-26,4,11)` | `7/26` | 7 |
+| C | `40,4,28,9/17` | `105,35,5,1` | `19/34,4/17,-1` | 34 | `(-34,8,19)` | `11/34` | 11 |
+
+Here `R_delta` is only the least common denominator of the displayed radii.
+An actual common Puiseux denominator may be a multiple after the missing root
+tails are supplied; then the integer `z`-order of every gap scales by the same
+factor.  The rational `t`-gaps are intrinsic.
+
+The representative-chain degree numbers
+
+```text
+a_r = n V_(r+1)/d_(r+1),    b_r = m V_(r+1)/d_(r+1)
+```
+
+are:
+
+| group | `(a_1,a_2,a_3)` for `g` | `(b_1,b_2,b_3)` for `f` |
+|---|---|---|
+| A | `(3,75,105)` | `(2,50,70)` |
+| B | `(3,90,105)` | `(2,60,70)` |
+| C | `(3,84,105)` | `(2,56,70)` |
+
+These give sizes along a distinguished chain.  As the framework stresses at
+lines 490-498, they do not give the full set partition of all leaves.
+
+### 3.1 Fixed star and normalization
+
+The reviewed normalized star is
+
+```text
+p_g(pi)=pi^3-pi,       p_f(pi)=pi^2-2/3.
+```
+
+It satisfies
+
+```text
+2 p_f p_g' - 3 p_g p_f' = 4/3 = kappa.
+```
+
+Because `kappa=cde/q`, retaining this exact normalization fixes the Jacobian
+constant rather than leaving it as `c=1`:
+
+| group | `q` | `c=kappa*q/(de)` |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| A | `1/2` | `1/9` |
+| B | `9/13` | `2/13` |
+| C | `9/17` | `2/17` |
+
+All are nonzero.  A run normalizing `c=1` would have to rescale `p_f`; it may
+not simultaneously claim the fixed star above unchanged.  In the target
+systems contemplated here `c` is specialized to the displayed nonzero
+constant, so it adds no intrinsic unknown.  A future unspecialized run must
+add one unknown and saturate at `c`.
+
+## 4. The maximum decoration justified by the inputs
+
+### 4.1 Partial rooted tree
+
+Each marked bottom star accounts for three `g`-leaves.  If, as a completion
+assumption, all marked stars are put inside the distinguished `D_2` cluster,
+the unresolved counts are:
+
+| group | `k` | marked `3k` | unmarked inside distinguished `D_2`: `a_2-3k` | outside that `D_2`: `105-a_2` |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| A | 12 | 36 | 39 | 30 |
+| A | 14 | 42 | 33 | 30 |
+| A | 16 | 48 | 27 | 30 |
+| A | 18 | 54 | 21 | 30 |
+| A | 20 | 60 | 15 | 30 |
+| A | 22 | 66 | 9 | 30 |
+| A | 24 | 72 | 3 | 30 |
+| B | 13 | 39 | 51 | 15 |
+| C | 17 | 51 | 33 | 21 |
+
+Even that containment is not route-to-tree data supplied by the census.  The
+table is an audit of how much remains to place, not a completed tree.
+
+### 4.2 Forced cyclic action on one nonzero packet
+
+For every group the bottom denominator increment is `A_1=2` and
+`Q_1=3=1*2+1`.  The stabilizer acts by `pi -> -pi`; the star roots split as
+the fixed root `{0}` and the pair `{-1,+1}`.
+
+At level two the data are:
+
+| group | `A_2` | `Q_2=V_3 d_2/d_3=u` | division | selected `V_2=1` branch |
+|---|---:|---:|---|---|
+| A | 18 | 25 | `25=1*18+7` | (10), nonzero root |
+| B | 13 | 30 | `30=2*13+4` | (10), nonzero root |
+| C | 17 | 28 | `28=1*17+11` | (10), nonzero root |
+
+Moh's automorphism mechanism, transcribed and explained at
+`census-rebase-opus5-20260902.md:137-149`, says a selected nonzero factor is
+accompanied by its full orbit of `A_2` distinct conjugate factors.  Let
+`zeta` be a primitive `R_delta`-th root, let
+`r_i=R_delta*delta_i`, choose a nonzero centre coefficient `b`, and write the
+shared ancestor prefix as `w_<delta2`.  The forced leading packet is
+
+```text
+tau_(j,c)(z)
+ = w_<delta2(zeta^j z)
+   + b zeta^(r_2 j) z^r_2
+   + c zeta^(r_1 j) z^r_1
+   + higher,
+
+j mod A_2,    c in {-1,0,+1}.
+```
+
+The three substitutions are:
+
+```text
+A: R=36, A_2=18, (r_2,r_1)=(14,21)
+B: R=26, A_2=13, (r_2,r_1)=(4,11)
+C: R=34, A_2=17, (r_2,r_1)=(8,19).
+```
+
+After `A_2` applications of `z -> zeta z`, the centre returns and
+`zeta^(r_1 A_2)=-1`, so `c` changes to `-c`.  Hence this marked packet has two
+orbits on **leaves**, of sizes `A_2` for `c=0` and `2A_2` for the combined
+nonzero leaves.  These leaf orbits must not be confused with the one orbit on
+bottom discs.
+
+At every later exponent `r`, honest shared coefficients must transform by
+
+```text
+u_(j+1,c,r) = zeta^r u_(j,c,r),
+```
+
+with the wrap sending `c` to `-c`.  Giving every branch an independent tail,
+or merely giving conjugate tails the same symbol without the character
+factor, is not this decoration.
+
+### 4.3 UNI and the requested “coarsest split”
+
+The arithmetic identity `N=k V_2 q`, together with `kV_2<=u`, yields the nine
+formal choices in the charge.  It is a capacity/integrality computation, not
+an orbit construction or attainment theorem.
+
+For the fixed nonzero branch (10), a complete minimal disc orbit has exactly
+`A_2` elements.  Therefore:
+
+* `A,k=18`, `B,k=13`, and `C,k=17` pass the **local `A_2` closure check** for
+  the one-orbit decoration.  They still lack a full 105-leaf decoration.
+* `A,k=12,14,16,20,22,24` are not complete orbits for the fixed level-two
+  action.  Passing them to the framework as verified `UNI` data would violate
+  its “partial orbit is an input error” rule.
+
+There is no second, canonically “coarsest” several-orbit decoration in the
+charged data.  The scalar level polynomial permits the numerical patterns
+
+```text
+A: 18 + residual fixed multiplicity 7
+B: 13 + 13 + residual fixed multiplicity 4
+C: 17 + residual fixed multiplicity 11.
+```
+
+The residual is multiplicity at the fixed zero of the scalar action, not that
+many distinct `V_2=1` bottom discs.  B's ambient level polynomial can contain
+two nonzero 13-orbits, but the second is outside the selected `k=13` packet
+and has no supplied major/minor or `q` data.  None of the selected packets
+contains two complete nonzero `A_2`-orbits.  Thus every requested `SPLIT` run
+is `OPEN[SPLIT-ORBIT-DATA]`; replacing it by singleton or “generic” orbits
+would be a new modelling convention.
+
+### 4.4 Every assumption and missing field
+
+The partial formula above assumes the marked star is the selected nonzero
+factor at the displayed level-two step, uses the least denominator of the
+three radii, fixes `b!=0`, fixes the star's affine/scalar normalization, and
+uses the natural cyclic action generated by `z -> zeta z`.  It does **not**
+assume that the remaining leaves are singletons or that unsupported tail
+coefficients vanish.
+
+A valid framework input still needs all of the following.
+
+1. A labelled rooted tree that places the `a_2-3k` unmarked leaves inside the
+   distinguished `D_2`, the `105-a_2` other leaves, and any other ancestor
+   clusters, with an ultrametric contact for every pair.
+2. The cyclic permutation and stabilizer on every residual leaf, plus an
+   explicit coefficient covariance check.  The bottom-disc label `UNI` does
+   not determine this permutation.
+3. Every centre coefficient in `w_<delta2`, every outer/minor leading
+   coefficient, and every tail coefficient capable of reaching the requested
+   moment order.
+4. The tame exponent semigroup.  The displayed `D_2` gap is a forced outer
+   activation; the charged review expressly warns that it need not be the
+   first exponent of each inner root tail.
+5. The equivalence/character relation for every shared coefficient at each
+   tree vertex.
+6. Nonzero separation leaders and discriminants for all strata, not only the
+   star discriminant.
+7. A finite last-supplied exponent sufficient to determine `D_i^-1` through
+   the residue and interpolation window.
+8. A value/definition for the adapter field `v`.  The D=105 census does not
+   print it; the sealed driver merely requires a nonnegative value.  Choosing
+   `v=0` would be an input adapter assumption, not a derived fact.
+9. If a condition on `g` alone rather than a fixed generic fibre is wanted,
+   target-independence over a transcendental `c_2`, modulo the one harmless
+   common additive constant.
+
+## 5. Exact system schema and order reached
+
+Once a complete decoration is supplied, the exact moment-form system is:
+
+```text
+D_i = product_(j != i) (tau_i-tau_j),       W_i=D_i^-1,
+[z^R] W_i = 0,                              NO-RESIDUE,
+q H_i[q] = -c R W_i[q+R]  (q != 0),         H_i[0]=a_orbit,
+M_r = sum_i H_i tau_i^r W_i.
+```
+
+At each retained exponent, the monic degree block is the 35-row family
+
+```text
+[z^q]M_r=0                 for r=0,...,33,
+[z^q](M_34-1)=0.
+```
+
+At a forbidden positive invariant exponent, polynomiality adds the 70 rows
+
+```text
+[z^q]M_r=0                 for r=35,...,104,
+```
+
+which is unit-triangularly equivalent to testing the remaining Lagrange
+coefficients after the already-counted monic identity.  Thus “35 equations
+per order” is only the DEG block.  A positive invariant global order normally
+has 105 DEG-plus-POLY slots before dependencies; NO-RESIDUE contributes `h`
+once when its guard is reached.
+
+The first nonvacuous global exponent is
+
+```text
+Q_* = first exponent in the invariant support at which one of
+      M_0,...,M_34-target or a forbidden tail is nonzero as a polynomial.
+```
+
+It cannot be read from `delta_1-delta_2`.  The junction number is provenance
+for activation of outer factors, while `Q_*` is an actual exponent of a
+global orbit trace.  In the minimal uniformizers the junction indices
+`7,7,11` are not multiples of `R=36,26,34`; a nontrivial character can cancel
+at the trace before influencing a later invariant order.  The complete
+templates decide which products do so.
+
+Accordingly the target order actually reached in this lane is:
+
+```text
+arithmetic/tree provenance:  D_2 gap reached exactly;
+restricted local equation:   D_2 gap reached exactly;
+global DEG/POLY emission:     no order reached (Q_* undefined);
+global rank/saturation:       not started because the input is invalid.
+```
+
+This is an input stop, not a timeout.  The bounded wrapper runs in under five
+seconds and under 70 MB.
+
+### 5.1 Exact restricted `D_2` operator
+
+Write
+
+```text
+phi=u_0+u_1 pi+u_2 pi^2,      gamma=v_0+v_1 pi+v_2 pi^2+v_3 pi^3,
+lambda_f=-2mu,                lambda_g=-3mu.
+```
+
+Linearizing LOCAL-KELLER at a correction of relative order `E` gives
+
+```text
+L_E(phi,gamma)
+ =(lambda_f+E)phi p_g' + lambda_f p_f gamma'
+  -(lambda_g+E)gamma p_f' - lambda_g p_g phi'.
+```
+
+In columns `(u_0,u_1,u_2,v_0,v_1,v_2,v_3)` and rows
+`(pi^0,...,pi^4)`, its exact matrix is
+
+```text
+[ 2mu-E       0        0        0       4mu/3      0       0 ]
+[   0       -E-mu      0      6mu-2E      0       8mu/3    0 ]
+[ 3E-6mu      0      -E-4mu     0      4mu-2E      0      4mu]
+[   0       3E-3mu     0        0         0      2mu-2E    0 ]
+[   0         0       3E        0         0         0     -2E]
+```
+
+Substitution gives:
+
+| group | `mu` | `E=delta_1-delta_2` | `E/mu` | rank | kernel | row cokernel |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| A | `1/12` | `7/36` | `7/3` | 5 | 2 | 0 |
+| B | `3/26` | `7/26` | `7/3` | 5 | 2 | 0 |
+| C | `3/34` | `11/34` | `11/3` | 5 | 2 | 0 |
+
+For A and B a kernel basis is
+
+```text
+(0,2/3,0,-1/3,0,1,0),
+(4/15,0,2/3,0,1/15,0,1).
+```
+
+For C the first vector is the same and the second is
+
+```text
+(4/3,0,2/3,0,5/3,0,1).
+```
+
+These ranks and bases are exact rational SymPy computations.  They establish
+only the restricted local two-parameter fibre.  Outer factors enlarge the
+coefficient spaces and then impose sharing; the global moments couple every
+disc and every residual leaf.
+
+## 6. Per-packet counts, ranks, cokernels, and ideals
+
+The blind table uses two local kernel coordinates independently on each of
+`k` discs and compares them with the 35 DEG slots.  Reproduced exactly:
+
+| group | `N` | `k` | restricted local coordinates `2k` | DEG slots | `35-2k` | blind overdetermination? |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| A | 6 | 12 | 24 | 35 | 11 | yes |
+| A | 7 | 14 | 28 | 35 | 7 | yes |
+| A | 8 | 16 | 32 | 35 | 3 | yes |
+| A | 9 | 18 | 36 | 35 | -1 | no |
+| A | 10 | 20 | 40 | 35 | -5 | no |
+| A | 11 | 22 | 44 | 35 | -9 | no |
+| A | 12 | 24 | 48 | 35 | -13 | no |
+| B | 9 | 13 | 26 | 35 | 9 | yes |
+| C | 9 | 17 | 34 | 35 | 1 | yes, the razor |
+
+This table is `COUNTING-BOUND` in the restricted model.  It is not even an
+intrinsic count for the complete system: orbit covariance can identify local
+coordinates, while centre, outer, minor, and shared-junction variables can
+add coordinates.  POLY can also add rows.  Only a decoration decides the net
+effect.
+
+The requested decoration/status table is:
+
+| group | `k` | `UNI` input status | `SPLIT` input status | global `U(4.13)` | global `C(4.11)` | global rank | global cokernel | saturated ideal / EMPTY | typed result |
+|---|---:|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| A | 12 | partial `A_2` orbit: input error | no supplied split | not computed | not computed | not computed | not computed | not formed | `COUNTING-BOUND` |
+| A | 14 | partial `A_2` orbit: input error | no supplied split | not computed | not computed | not computed | not computed | not formed | `COUNTING-BOUND` |
+| A | 16 | partial `A_2` orbit: input error | no supplied split | not computed | not computed | not computed | not computed | not formed | `COUNTING-BOUND` |
+| A | 18 | local orbit closes; full tree missing | no distinct selected multi-orbit split | not computed | not computed | not computed | not computed | not formed | `COUNTING-BOUND` |
+| A | 20 | partial `A_2` orbit: input error | no supplied split | not computed | not computed | not computed | not computed | not formed | `COUNTING-BOUND` |
+| A | 22 | partial `A_2` orbit: input error | no supplied split | not computed | not computed | not computed | not computed | not formed | `COUNTING-BOUND` |
+| A | 24 | partial `A_2` orbit: input error | no supplied split | not computed | not computed | not computed | not computed | not formed | `COUNTING-BOUND` |
+| B | 13 | local orbit closes; full tree missing | second 13-orbit is outside selected packet | not computed | not computed | not computed | not computed | not formed | `COUNTING-BOUND` |
+| C | 17 | local orbit closes; full tree missing | no distinct selected multi-orbit split | not computed | not computed | not computed | not computed | not formed | `COUNTING-BOUND` |
+
+The driver emits 18 manifest records, one for each table row and each of
+`UNI/SPLIT`, with the same result type.  A status of “local orbit closes” is
+not `SURVIVES-TO-Q`; no global equation has been tested.
+
+### 6.1 Why no saturated ideal was attempted
+
+A target saturation requires a declared coefficient field, polynomial ring,
+generator order, the ideal component, and the localization product containing
+all discriminants, unit leaders, `c`, and degree leaders.  The outer
+discriminants and leaders are among the missing decoration data, and there is
+no target ideal to extract.  Running `sat()` on a list of symbolic names would
+violate the campaign guardrail.  Therefore `EMPTY=NOT COMPUTED` on all target
+rows.
+
+No result is typed `RANK-EXCESS`: an ambient generic rank away from the target
+variety would not supply componentwise codimension.  No result is typed
+`SATURATED-EMPTY`: the localized ideal was not formed.  No result is typed
+`SURVIVES-TO-Q`: absence of a test is not passage through a test.
+
+## 7. Controls in the same bounded run
+
+### 7.1 Sealed suite
+
+The frozen driver reproduced:
+
+```text
+controls: 40 checks, 0 failures
+selftest: 50 checks, 0 failures
+```
+
+Its small emitter example also reproduces the warning against raw counting:
+36 raw lifted equations, 35 deduplicated equations, 27 lifted unknowns, but
+ambient symbolic Jacobian rank only 26.  Raw excess is not rank excess.
+
+### 7.2 Requested positive controls and free parameters
+
+The wrapper reruns exact quotient-ring interpolation after adding a symbolic
+common constant `a`.  It obtains:
+
+| pair | exact recovered interpolant | branch-orbit constant before gauge | after fixing common additive gauge | status at `7/36,7/26,11/34` |
+|---|---|---:|---:|---|
+| `(y,x+y^3)` | `y+a` | 1 | 0 | `SURVIVES-TO-Q` |
+| `(y,x+y^5)` | `y+a` | 1 | 0 | `SURVIVES-TO-Q` |
+| `(x+y^5,y+(x+y^5)^3)` | `x+y^5+a` | 1 | 0 | `SURVIVES-TO-Q` |
+
+The first two branch sets are transitive under `mu_3` and `mu_5`.  The
+composition's 15 branches are transitive under `mu_15` and form five bottom
+discs of three branches.  The exact interpolants and NO-RESIDUE identities
+hold to all orders, so passing at the three listed rational orders is not a
+truncation accident.
+
+### 7.3 Target-independent negative control
+
+For
+
+```text
+g=y^2-x^2-x,
+tau_+ = (x^2+x+c_2)^(1/2),    tau_-=-tau_+,
+```
+
+the coefficients of `x^-1=t^1` in `1/g_y(tau_+)` and
+`1/g_y(tau_-)` are `+1/2` and `-1/2`.  The failure is independent of the
+target, and the wrapper reports exactly `failure_order_t=1`.
+
+### 7.4 Vacuity mutation and saturation control
+
+For the passing cubic shear take `x=z^-3` and roots
+
+```text
+-z^-1,
+(1+sqrt(3)I)z^-1/2,
+(1-sqrt(3)I)z^-1/2.
+```
+
+Mutate only the first tame coefficient:
+
+```text
+tau_0 -> -z^-1+a,       tau_1,tau_2 unchanged.
+```
+
+The three `[z^3](1/D_i)` coefficients change from zero to
+
+```text
+a/3,
+-I a (sqrt(3)-3I)/18,
+ I a (sqrt(3)+3I)/18.
+```
+
+Thus the mutation fails at `z^3=t^1`.  To prevent the nominal mutation
+`a=0` from masquerading as a negative test, the wrapper declares the exact
+ring and Rabinowitsch localization
+
+```text
+ring:  QQ[a,sat_witness], lex(a,sat_witness)
+ideal: <a/3, sat_witness*a-1>.
+```
+
+Its Groebner basis is `[1]`, so the mutated open stratum `a!=0` is empty.
+This is `SATURATED-EMPTY` for the mutation control only, not for a D=105
+target.  The mutation is a branch-series vacuity guard; no claim is made that
+the mutated roots come from a new polynomial map.
+
+## 8. Reading the result
+
+### 8.1 Does the first global order overdetermine?
+
+For the **blind restricted count**, A is overdetermined at `k=12,14,16` and
+not at `k=18,20,22,24`; B is overdetermined by 9; C is overdetermined by 1.
+That faithfully reproduces the charged GPT-5.5 table.
+
+For the **exact global system**, the answer is `UNDECIDED` for A, B, and C.
+There is no known `Q_*`, no intrinsic `U(Q_*)`, and no instantiated
+`C(Q_*)`.  At a positive invariant order POLY may add 70 rows, while outer and
+shared variables may add columns.  Galois descent may remove repetitions and
+identify parameters.  One cannot select only whichever side helps a kill.
+
+C's `34`-versus-`35` razor is therefore a well-motivated experiment design,
+not a computed cokernel.  In the restricted 35-by-34 fiction, full column
+rank would leave a row cokernel of at least one.  The actual global matrix may
+have more or fewer intrinsic columns and dependent rows.
+
+### 8.2 What a rank dependency would mean
+
+A dependency means that a nominal coefficient condition does not cut a new
+tangent direction on the component being tested.  Possible sources include a
+universal root identity, a Galois repetition, a common-additive gauge,
+character cancellation, an ancestor-sharing identity, or a relation special
+to the star/outer coefficients.  For C, one exact dependency in a genuine
+35-by-34 descended matrix would remove the count razor and identify a
+structural compatibility to propagate to later orders.  It would not by
+itself prove existence or all-order survival.
+
+Conversely, a sampled ambient rank at arbitrary values of algebraically
+related star and root-of-unity parameters is not a rank on a solution
+component.  It cannot be promoted to a kill without the ring map and component
+check.
+
+### 8.3 What `SATURATED-EMPTY` would buy
+
+If, after enumerating every actual decoration/component of A, B, and C, each
+ideal saturated at the full nondegenerate product were empty, all three true
+`D=105` groups would be killed.  Since the rebased census identifies 105 as
+the smallest surviving degree above 100 and the next surviving degree is 108,
+the conclusion would be only
+
+```text
+D_min >= 108.
+```
+
+It would not prove a uniform degree theorem or the Jacobian conjecture.  This
+lane has no such emptiness result, so even that limited conclusion is not
+available here.
+
+## 9. Bounded OPENs
+
+1. `OPEN[D105-FULL-DECORATION]`.  Bounded quantity: for the nine charged
+   `(group,k)` choices, place and label exactly 105 roots, specify all pairwise
+   contacts through the first invariant order and the `D_2` guard, give the
+   cyclic permutation/covariance and sharing classes, and provide all needed
+   coefficients.  The three locally closed packets require respectively 51,
+   66, and 54 residual leaves outside their marked stars; the six other A
+   `UNI` requests additionally need a replacement for the failed `A_2`
+   closure.
+2. `OPEN[SPLIT-ORBIT-DATA]`.  Bounded quantity: nine requested split packet
+   decorations.  The `d_j` chain supplies no canonical several-orbit
+   partition.  For the selected packets no `k` contains two complete nonzero
+   `A_2` orbits; any alternative must arrive with new branch types and
+   `q,V_2` data.
+3. `OPEN[D105-GLOBAL-RANK-AND-SATURATION]`.  Bounded quantity: at most 18
+   requested decorated systems, once the preceding inputs exist.  For each,
+   compute the first invariant coefficient and continue through `D_2`; print
+   intrinsic `U,C`, exact or certified lower-bound rank, row cokernel, the
+   declared localized ring, and ideal emptiness.  No part of this OPEN is
+   discharged by the local rank-5 calculation.
+
+## 10. FALLACY-v2 audit
+
+* **Flag/place/series.**  A bottom disc, one of its three root series, the
+  level-two scalar factor, and a physical place are kept distinct.  `J_2` is
+  an activation gap, not automatically a global coefficient order.
+* **Per-ray/exit-set charge.**  No exit price or exit set is asserted.  Hence
+  no `charge_basis` line is due.
+* **Carrier/attainment.**  The census permits the nine arithmetic `k` values;
+  it does not attain their full trees.  Local `A_2` closure for three packets
+  is not full attainment.
+* **Floor/attainment.**  `2k` versus 35 is a restricted count, not rank,
+  cokernel, height, emptiness, or an exact global unknown count.
+* **`sat()` wrapping.**  No target saturation is called without an ideal.
+  The mutation control explicitly declares `QQ[a,sat_witness]`, its generator
+  order, ideal, localization equation, and positive/negative role.
+* **Raw remainder degree.**  The exact controls use quotient-ring remainders
+  in the declared fibre polynomial.  No vanished target leader is normalized
+  away.
+* **Variable/ring map.**  The target ring is deliberately not invented.  The
+  fixed-star choice and its three values of `c` are printed.
+* **Prime label/derivative.**  Primes in the local operator mean `d/dpi`;
+  branch integration is `d/dx`.  `A_1,A_2` are denominator increments, not
+  Lagrange coefficients.
+* **Merge-free/M-descent.**  No M-descent or merge-free claim is made.
+* **Target/arrival index.**  The fixed group labels and `D_2` level are kept
+  separate from actual incoming coefficient order `Q_*`, which is missing.
+
