+# D105-RANK-GATE — preflight, forced packet decoration, and the missing global matrix
+
+**Lane/date.** `D105-RANK-GATE`, 2026-09-03.  **Status of new work:**
+`PROVED-HERE / UNREVIEWED` unless a narrower type is printed.  No canonical
+ledger was edited and `jc2-lean` was not inspected.
+
+## 0. Executive verdict
+
+The requested global ranks, cokernels, and saturated ideals are **not defined
+by the charged inputs**.  I therefore do not report a fabricated rank for any
+of the three true `D=105` groups.
+
+The obstruction is concrete.  Section 4.1 of the sealed framework requires a
+rooted tree on all 105 labelled roots, a checked cyclic action on those roots,
+every root's truncated Puiseux series, the sharing relations among tame
+coefficients, and a precision guard.  The census supplies a representative
+Moh chain and a capacity for bottom discs.  The reviewed star supplies the
+three relative leading coefficients `{-1,0,1}` inside one bottom disc.  It does
+not supply the other roots, the disc centres, their contacts, their tail
+support, or their sharing.  Those missing quantities occur in the first
+global moment matrix itself.
+
+There are nevertheless four exact outputs.
+
+1. The three chains, radii, denominator increments, representative cluster
+   sizes, minimal junction orders, and normalized Jacobian constants are
+   reconstructed exactly.
+2. The denominator increments give order-`A_2=18,13,17` orbits of nonzero
+   **factors of the local cover polynomial `p(pi)`**.  They do not identify
+   those factors with physical bottom discs or global fibre branches.  Thus
+   they neither validate nor invalidate any requested `k`-disc `UNI` packet;
+   all nine `UNI` actions and all nine `SPLIT` actions still need
+   route-to-tree data.
+3. At the `D_2` gap, the exact restricted one-disc operator has rank 5,
+   kernel dimension 2, and cokernel dimension 0 for every group.  This
+   verifies the local source of GPT-5.5's `2k` count.  It does not construct
+   the 35-row global map.
+4. The sealed controls reproduce `40/0` and the selftest `50/0`.  The three
+   requested positive controls pass identically, hence at every charged
+   junction order, with one common additive parameter before gauge fixing.
+   The target-independent bad `g` fails at `t^1`.  A Galois-covariant
+   one-parameter mutation of the cubic root tails fails the polynomial-input
+   guard at `t^1`; saturation at the mutation parameter gives the unit ideal.
+
+For every requested `(group,k,UNI/SPLIT)` row the only licensed target verdict
+is `COUNTING-BOUND`.  No row earns `RANK-EXCESS`, `SATURATED-EMPTY`, or
+`SURVIVES-TO-Q`, because no complete target system was emitted.  Consequently
+there is **no D=105 kill and no change to `D_min`** in this lane.
+
+## 1. Custody and hash gate
+
+The mandatory gate was run before opening any frozen input.  All eight hashes
+matched exactly:
+
+```text
+20d554a0b19c563093ec35caad58664f800d7517490f530a07f511d7042393b6  global-interpolation-sol56-20260902.md
+49ba5a019714e30a952c998fb39a88aff38505a80fcac6df3c5883bb16599588  globalinterp.py
+fb137b92d88b2f59f369bbffb2a0591aed69e9294135751c329da9eea58f6948  census-rebase-opus5-20260902.md
+47f59906927ff9d2b38b25b11c2e46cef3c472b3d8db300f12c12f22906848e1  survivors-D48-120.txt
+5e1646f507e946b831dcb77d542f7ab367eb398227a3032b96bcd7a45d2f320d  ideation-20260903T1015Z-gpt55.md
+9e485492940818ea25b955af1713de53bc823af78f9f00a8991aaba9372f527d  time-function-endgame-review-sol56-20260902.md
+69ff5bdea265adc37c9518f381eccfe6a6162c430a51075b6c2069f709894473  bottomode.py
+d20bf0841a1ba2b229d423bb948e6c4474a4f5a83f55148071cae39cb6c506c2  moh_skeleton_full.py
+```
+
+Only those frozen copies and the new files in
+`box/d105rank-drivers-20260903/` were read.  In particular, no other
+`ideation-20260903T1015Z-*` file and no other running lane report was read.
+
+The frozen census lists the three rows at
+`census-rebase-opus5-20260902.md:474-487`; the compact charged listing
+independently gives the same rows at `survivors-D48-120.txt:5-8`.  The blind
+count is at `ideation-20260903T1015Z-gpt55.md:117-181`.  The framework's
+information obstruction and exact decorated-input contract are at
+`global-interpolation-sol56-20260902.md:461-514`.
+
+## 2. What the sealed framework actually requires
+
+Put `t=x^-1` and choose a common field `C((z))` with `x=z^-R`.  For a requested
+last exponent `Q`, the report's decorated skeleton is
+
+```text
+D_Q = (bare Moh tuple,
+       rooted cluster tree on n labelled leaves,
+       cyclic Galois action and orbit/stabilizer data,
+       truncated Puiseux template tau_i(z) for every leaf,
+       declarations identifying shared tame coefficients,
+       Q and a sufficient valuation guard).
+```
+
+This contract is substantive, not serialization overhead.  If
+`D_i=product_(j!=i)(tau_i-tau_j)`, then every entry of `D_i^-1`, every time
+value, and every moment sees contacts with all other 104 roots.  A missing
+outer leaf can change a denominator leader, the first retained exponent, a
+residue, a moment coefficient, and the rank.
+
+For a complete decoration the intrinsic unknown count is
+
+```text
+U(Q) = h + u_0 + |Z_Q|,                                    (4.13)
+```
+
+where `h` is the number of branch orbits, `u_0` is the number of
+unspecialized leading/star parameters after gauges, and `Z_Q` is the set of
+independent tame symbols that can reach the equations through the complete
+inverse/integration guard.  None of `h`, `u_0`, or `Z_Q` follows from `k`.
+In particular, “one orbit of bottom discs” does not by itself give the number
+of orbits on the 105 leaves, and two local kernel coordinates per displayed
+disc are not formula (4.13).
+
+Likewise the intrinsic equation count is
+
+```text
+C(Q) = C_res + C_deg(Q) + C_poly(Q),                        (4.11)
+C_res = h.
+```
+
+Its `C_deg` summands require the initial exponents of the 35 moment identities;
+its `C_poly` summands require the initial exponents of the surviving
+coefficients.  Those exponents are absent here.  The normalized shortcut
+`C=h+35+105K` applies only after one has proved the stationary invariant
+support `t^0,...,t^K`; it cannot be used to invent that support.
+
+### 2.1 Implementation audit of `globalinterp.py`
+
+The sealed implementation is valuable for custody of the exact finite
+straight-line lift and for the controls, but it cannot silently repair the
+missing decoration.
+
+* It requires exactly `n` branch objects, yet it has no JSON object for a
+  rooted tree, cyclic permutation, stabilizer, or sharing equivalence
+  relation.  It infers pairwise contacts and trusts an orbit's
+  `verified=true` flag.
+* A direct probe changed its passing two-branch example from the equivariant
+  pair `I z^-1,-I z^-1` to `I z^-1,-2I z^-1`, retained `verified=true`, and
+  the driver accepted it, reduced NO-RESIDUE to one effective row, and reused
+  one integration constant.  A D=105 wrapper must therefore validate
+  covariance before invoking the sealed orbit shortcut.
+* Its reported unknown count includes product, inverse, power, time, and
+  polynomial-coefficient auxiliaries.  It is not (4.13).  Its reported rank
+  is the ambient Jacobian rank of that lifted system, not the rank of the
+  descended intrinsic moment map at a solution.
+* It orbit-reduces only the metadata count for NO-RESIDUE; it does not project
+  all equations to the trivial character before ranking.
+* It lists inequations but has no saturation or ideal-emptiness routine.
+* Missing exact coefficients are interpreted as zero; `tail_from` creates an
+  unlimited free tail.  There is no independent finite “last supplied
+  coefficient” with which to certify a genuinely truncated algebraic input.
+
+The unsymmetrized lift is also the wrong computational representation for
+this target.  At one coefficient it already has `105*104=10,920` prefix
+products, 105 inverses, and at least `105*69=7,245` nontrivial power nodes.
+For the driver's illustrative `tau_i=(i+1)z^-1`, `m=70`, `qmax=0` recurrence,
+the power count is 514,395 before time and evaluation equations.  This is why
+the next valid implementation should form the 35 character-projected moments
+directly.  The present lane was stopped for missing mathematical input before
+spending the 30-minute/6-GB allowance on a matrix for a synthetic completion.
+
+## 3. Exact arithmetic forced by the three groups
+
+For all groups, `n=105`, `m=70`, `K=35`, `(d,e)=(2,3)`, `V_2=1`, and
+`M_1=-70`, `M_3=103`.  Applying the frozen implementation of Moh's radius
+formula gives:
+
+| group | `M_2,V_3,u,q` | `d_1,d_2,d_3,d_4` | `delta_1,delta_2,delta_3` | minimal `R_delta` | `(R delta_3,R delta_2,R delta_1)` | `J_2/R = delta_1-delta_2` | minimal `J_2` |
+|---|---|---|---|---:|---|---|---:|
+| A | `28,5,25,1/2` | `105,35,7,1` | `7/12,7/18,-1` | 36 | `(-36,14,21)` | `7/36` | 7 |
+| B | `28,6,30,9/13` | `105,35,7,1` | `11/26,2/13,-1` | 26 | `(-26,4,11)` | `7/26` | 7 |
+| C | `40,4,28,9/17` | `105,35,5,1` | `19/34,4/17,-1` | 34 | `(-34,8,19)` | `11/34` | 11 |
+
+Here `R_delta` is only the least common denominator of the displayed radii.
+An actual common Puiseux denominator may be a multiple after the missing root
+tails are supplied; then the integer `z`-order of every gap scales by the same
+factor.  The rational `t`-gaps are intrinsic.
+
+The representative-chain degree numbers
+
+```text
+a_r = n V_(r+1)/d_(r+1),    b_r = m V_(r+1)/d_(r+1)
+```
+
+are:
+
+| group | `(a_1,a_2,a_3)` for `g` | `(b_1,b_2,b_3)` for `f` |
+|---|---|---|
+| A | `(3,75,105)` | `(2,50,70)` |
+| B | `(3,90,105)` | `(2,60,70)` |
+| C | `(3,84,105)` | `(2,56,70)` |
+
+These give sizes along a distinguished chain.  As the framework stresses at
+lines 490-498, they do not give the full set partition of all leaves.
+
+### 3.1 Fixed star and normalization
+
+The reviewed normalized star is
+
+```text
+p_g(pi)=pi^3-pi,       p_f(pi)=pi^2-2/3.
+```
+
+It satisfies
+
+```text
+2 p_f p_g' - 3 p_g p_f' = 4/3 = kappa.
+```
+
+Because `kappa=cde/q`, retaining this exact normalization fixes the Jacobian
+constant rather than leaving it as `c=1`:
+
+| group | `q` | `c=kappa*q/(de)` |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| A | `1/2` | `1/9` |
+| B | `9/13` | `2/13` |
+| C | `9/17` | `2/17` |
+
+All are nonzero.  A run normalizing `c=1` would have to rescale `p_f`; it may
+not simultaneously claim the fixed star above unchanged.  In the target
+systems contemplated here `c` is specialized to the displayed nonzero
+constant, so it adds no intrinsic unknown.  A future unspecialized run must
+add one unknown and saturate at `c`.
+
+## 4. The maximum decoration justified by the inputs
+
+### 4.1 Partial rooted tree
+
+Each marked bottom star accounts for three `g`-leaves.  If, as a completion
+assumption, all marked stars are put inside the distinguished `D_2` cluster,
+the unresolved counts are:
+
+| group | `k` | marked `3k` | unmarked inside distinguished `D_2`: `a_2-3k` | outside that `D_2`: `105-a_2` |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| A | 12 | 36 | 39 | 30 |
+| A | 14 | 42 | 33 | 30 |
+| A | 16 | 48 | 27 | 30 |
+| A | 18 | 54 | 21 | 30 |
+| A | 20 | 60 | 15 | 30 |
+| A | 22 | 66 | 9 | 30 |
+| A | 24 | 72 | 3 | 30 |
+| B | 13 | 39 | 51 | 15 |
+| C | 17 | 51 | 33 | 21 |
+
+Even that containment is not route-to-tree data supplied by the census.  The
+table is an audit of how much remains to place, not a completed tree.
+
+### 4.2 Cover-polynomial action and a conditional series ansatz
+
+For every group the bottom denominator increment is `A_1=2` and
+`Q_1=3=1*2+1`.  The stabilizer acts by `pi -> -pi`; the star roots split as
+the fixed root `{0}` and the pair `{-1,+1}`.
+
+At level two the data are:
+
+| group | `A_2` | `Q_2=V_3 d_2/d_3=u` | division | selected `V_2=1` branch |
+|---|---:|---:|---|---|
+| A | 18 | 25 | `25=1*18+7` | (10), nonzero root |
+| B | 13 | 30 | `30=2*13+4` | (10), nonzero root |
+| C | 17 | 28 | `28=1*17+11` | (10), nonzero root |
+
+Moh's automorphism mechanism, transcribed and explained at
+`census-rebase-opus5-20260902.md:137-149`, says a selected nonzero factor of
+the relevant local cover polynomial `p(pi)` is accompanied by its full orbit
+of `A_2` distinct conjugate factors.  It does **not** say that these factors
+are `A_2` physical bottom discs or `A_2` branches of `g-c_2`.
+
+For bookkeeping only, one can make the following conditional ansatz.  Assume
+a route identifying a copy of each cover factor with a star-bearing series
+packet; let `zeta` be a primitive `R_delta`-th root, put
+`r_i=R_delta*delta_i`, choose `b!=0`, and write the shared ancestor prefix as
+`w_<delta2`.  Then a covariant formal copy would be
+
+```text
+tau_(j,c)(z)
+ = w_<delta2(zeta^j z)
+   + b zeta^(r_2 j) z^r_2
+   + c zeta^(r_1 j) z^r_1
+   + higher,
+
+j mod A_2,    c in {-1,0,+1}.
+```
+
+The three substitutions are:
+
+```text
+A: R=36, A_2=18, (r_2,r_1)=(14,21)
+B: R=26, A_2=13, (r_2,r_1)=(4,11)
+C: R=34, A_2=17, (r_2,r_1)=(8,19).
+```
+
+Within this ansatz, after `A_2` applications of `z -> zeta z`, the formal
+centre returns and `zeta^(r_1 A_2)=-1`, so `c` changes to `-c`.  Its **series
+labels** would therefore cycle with sizes `A_2` for `c=0` and `2A_2` for the
+combined nonzero labels.  These are not promoted as leaf or disc orbits.  The
+missing route-to-tree theorem is exactly what would be needed to make that
+identification.
+
+If this ansatz is used as a synthetic model, later coefficients must transform
+by
+
+```text
+u_(j+1,c,r) = zeta^r u_(j,c,r),
+```
+
+with the wrap sending `c` to `-c`.  Giving every formal copy an independent
+tail, or merely giving conjugate tails the same symbol without the character
+factor, would not even realize this conditional action.
+
+### 4.3 UNI and the requested “coarsest split”
+
+The arithmetic identity `N=k V_2 q`, together with `kV_2<=u`, yields the nine
+formal choices in the charge.  It is a capacity/integrality computation, not
+an orbit construction or attainment theorem.  The requested `UNI` decoration
+adds the assumption “these `k` physical bottom discs form one orbit,” but the
+charged data contains neither the permutation nor its covariance on the 105
+root series.  Consequently **all nine UNI decorations remain open inputs**.
+The coincidences `k=A_2` in A/18, B/13, and C/17 are suggestive numerical
+compatibilities only; matching cardinalities do not give a map from cover
+factors to discs.
+
+There is no second, canonically “coarsest” several-orbit decoration in the
+charged data.  The scalar level polynomial permits the numerical patterns
+
+```text
+A: 18 + residual fixed multiplicity 7
+B: 13 + 13 + residual fixed multiplicity 4
+C: 17 + residual fixed multiplicity 11.
+```
+
+The residual is multiplicity at the fixed zero of the scalar action, not that
+many distinct `V_2=1` bottom discs.  B's cover polynomial can contain two
+nonzero 13-orbits, but there is no licensed identification of either with the
+selected `k=13` disc packet and no supplied major/minor or `q` data for a
+second physical packet.  Thus every requested `SPLIT` run is
+`OPEN[SPLIT-ORBIT-DATA]`; replacing it by singleton or “generic” disc orbits
+would be a new modelling convention.
+
+### 4.4 Every assumption and missing field
+
+The partial formula above assumes the marked star is the selected nonzero
+factor at the displayed level-two step, uses the least denominator of the
+three radii, fixes `b!=0`, fixes the star's affine/scalar normalization, and
+uses the natural cyclic action generated by `z -> zeta z`.  It does **not**
+assume that the remaining leaves are singletons or that unsupported tail
+coefficients vanish.
+
+A valid framework input still needs all of the following.
+
+1. A labelled rooted tree that places the `a_2-3k` unmarked leaves inside the
+   distinguished `D_2`, the `105-a_2` other leaves, and any other ancestor
+   clusters, with an ultrametric contact for every pair.
+2. The cyclic permutation and stabilizer on every residual leaf, plus an
+   explicit coefficient covariance check.  The bottom-disc label `UNI` does
+   not determine this permutation.
+3. Every centre coefficient in `w_<delta2`, every outer/minor leading
+   coefficient, and every tail coefficient capable of reaching the requested
+   moment order.
+4. The tame exponent semigroup.  The displayed `D_2` gap is a forced outer
+   activation; the charged review expressly warns that it need not be the
+   first exponent of each inner root tail.
+5. The equivalence/character relation for every shared coefficient at each
+   tree vertex.
+6. Nonzero separation leaders and discriminants for all strata, not only the
+   star discriminant.
+7. A finite last-supplied exponent sufficient to determine `D_i^-1` through
+   the residue and interpolation window.
+8. A value/definition for the adapter field `v`.  The D=105 census does not
+   print it; the sealed driver merely requires a nonnegative value.  Choosing
+   `v=0` would be an input adapter assumption, not a derived fact.
+9. If a condition on `g` alone rather than a fixed generic fibre is wanted,
+   target-independence over a transcendental `c_2`, modulo the one harmless
+   common additive constant.
+
+## 5. Exact system schema and order reached
+
+Once a complete decoration is supplied, the exact moment-form system is:
+
+```text
+D_i = product_(j != i) (tau_i-tau_j),       W_i=D_i^-1,
+[z^R] W_i = 0,                              NO-RESIDUE,
+q H_i[q] = -c R W_i[q+R]  (q != 0),         H_i[0]=a_orbit,
+M_r = sum_i H_i tau_i^r W_i.
+```
+
+At each retained exponent, the monic degree block is the 35-row family
+
+```text
+[z^q]M_r=0                 for r=0,...,33,
+[z^q](M_34-1)=0.
+```
+
+At a forbidden positive invariant exponent, polynomiality adds the 70 rows
+
+```text
+[z^q]M_r=0                 for r=35,...,104,
+```
+
+which is unit-triangularly equivalent to testing the remaining Lagrange
+coefficients after the already-counted monic identity.  Thus “35 equations
+per order” is only the DEG block.  A positive invariant global order normally
+has 105 DEG-plus-POLY slots before dependencies; NO-RESIDUE contributes `h`
+once when its guard is reached.
+
+The first nonvacuous global exponent is
+
+```text
+Q_* = first exponent in the invariant support at which one of
+      M_0,...,M_34-target or a forbidden tail is nonzero as a polynomial.
+```
+
+It cannot be read from `delta_1-delta_2`.  The junction number is provenance
+for activation of outer factors, while `Q_*` is an actual exponent of a
+global orbit trace.  In the minimal uniformizers the junction indices
+`7,7,11` are not multiples of `R=36,26,34`; a nontrivial character can cancel
+at the trace before influencing a later invariant order.  The complete
+templates decide which products do so.
+
+Accordingly the target order actually reached in this lane is:
+
+```text
+arithmetic/tree provenance:  D_2 gap reached exactly;
+restricted local equation:   D_2 gap reached exactly;
+global DEG/POLY emission:     no order reached (Q_* undefined);
+global rank/saturation:       not started because the input is invalid.
+```
+
+This is an input stop, not a timeout.  The bounded wrapper runs in under five
+seconds and under 70 MB.
+
+### 5.1 Exact restricted `D_2` operator
+
+Write
+
+```text
+phi=u_0+u_1 pi+u_2 pi^2,      gamma=v_0+v_1 pi+v_2 pi^2+v_3 pi^3,
+lambda_f=-2mu,                lambda_g=-3mu.
+```
+
+Linearizing LOCAL-KELLER at a correction of relative order `E` gives
+
+```text
+L_E(phi,gamma)
+ =(lambda_f+E)phi p_g' + lambda_f p_f gamma'
+  -(lambda_g+E)gamma p_f' - lambda_g p_g phi'.
+```
+
+In columns `(u_0,u_1,u_2,v_0,v_1,v_2,v_3)` and rows
+`(pi^0,...,pi^4)`, its exact matrix is
+
+```text
+[ 2mu-E       0        0        0       4mu/3      0       0 ]
+[   0       -E-mu      0      6mu-2E      0       8mu/3    0 ]
+[ 3E-6mu      0      -E-4mu     0      4mu-2E      0      4mu]
+[   0       3E-3mu     0        0         0      2mu-2E    0 ]
+[   0         0       3E        0         0         0     -2E]
+```
+
+Substitution gives:
+
+| group | `mu` | `E=delta_1-delta_2` | `E/mu` | rank | kernel | row cokernel |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| A | `1/12` | `7/36` | `7/3` | 5 | 2 | 0 |
+| B | `3/26` | `7/26` | `7/3` | 5 | 2 | 0 |
+| C | `3/34` | `11/34` | `11/3` | 5 | 2 | 0 |
+
+For A and B a kernel basis is
+
+```text
+(0,2/3,0,-1/3,0,1,0),
+(4/15,0,2/3,0,1/15,0,1).
+```
+
+For C the first vector is the same and the second is
+
+```text
+(4/3,0,2/3,0,5/3,0,1).
+```
+
+These ranks and bases are exact rational SymPy computations.  They establish
+only the restricted local two-parameter fibre.  Outer factors enlarge the
+coefficient spaces and then impose sharing; the global moments couple every
+disc and every residual leaf.
+
