+### 3.1 Fixed star and normalization
+
+The reviewed normalized star is
+
+```text
+p_g(pi)=pi^3-pi,       p_f(pi)=pi^2-2/3.
+```
+
+It satisfies
+
+```text
+2 p_f p_g' - 3 p_g p_f' = 4/3 = kappa.
+```
+
+Because `kappa=cde/q`, retaining this exact normalization fixes the Jacobian
+constant rather than leaving it as `c=1`:
+
+| group | `q` | `c=kappa*q/(de)` |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| A | `1/2` | `1/9` |
+| B | `9/13` | `2/13` |
+| C | `9/17` | `2/17` |
+
+All are nonzero.  A run normalizing `c=1` would have to rescale `p_f`; it may
+not simultaneously claim the fixed star above unchanged.  In the target
+systems contemplated here `c` is specialized to the displayed nonzero
+constant, so it adds no intrinsic unknown.  A future unspecialized run must
+add one unknown and saturate at `c`.
