+
+The driver emits 18 manifest records, one for each table row and each of
+`UNI/SPLIT`, with the same result type.  An assumed `UNI` cardinality is not
+`SURVIVES-TO-Q`; no global equation has been tested.
+
+### 6.1 Why no saturated ideal was attempted
+
+A target saturation requires a declared coefficient field, polynomial ring,
+generator order, the ideal component, and the localization product containing
+all discriminants, unit leaders, `c`, and degree leaders.  The outer
+discriminants and leaders are among the missing decoration data, and there is
+no target ideal to extract.  Running `sat()` on a list of symbolic names would
+violate the campaign guardrail.  Therefore `EMPTY=NOT COMPUTED` on all target
+rows.
+
+No result is typed `RANK-EXCESS`: an ambient generic rank away from the target
+variety would not supply componentwise codimension.  No result is typed
+`SATURATED-EMPTY`: the localized ideal was not formed.  No result is typed
+`SURVIVES-TO-Q`: absence of a test is not passage through a test.
+
+## 7. Controls in the same bounded run
+
+### 7.1 Sealed suite
+
+The frozen driver reproduced:
+
+```text
+controls: 40 checks, 0 failures
+selftest: 50 checks, 0 failures
+```
+
+Its small emitter example also reproduces the warning against raw counting:
+36 raw lifted equations, 35 deduplicated equations, 27 lifted unknowns, but
+ambient symbolic Jacobian rank only 26.  Raw excess is not rank excess.
+
+### 7.2 Requested positive controls and free parameters
+
+The wrapper reruns the sealed analytic automorphism controls and also checks
+the exact quotient-ring remainder after adding a symbolic common constant
+`a`.  This is an all-order identity, not a finite decorated-emitter rank or a
+measurement of free root-tail parameters.  It obtains:
+
+| pair | exact recovered interpolant | branch-orbit constant before gauge | after fixing common additive gauge | status at `7/36,7/26,11/34` |
+|---|---|---:|---:|---|
+| `(y,x+y^3)` | `y+a` | 1 | 0 | `SURVIVES-TO-Q` |
+| `(y,x+y^5)` | `y+a` | 1 | 0 | `SURVIVES-TO-Q` |
+| `(x+y^5,y+(x+y^5)^3)` | `x+y^5+a` | 1 | 0 | `SURVIVES-TO-Q` |
+
+The first two exact branch sets are transitive under `mu_3` and `mu_5`.  The
+composition's 15 branches are transitive under `mu_15` and form five bottom
+discs of three branches.  The exact interpolants and NO-RESIDUE identities
+hold to all orders, so passing at the three listed rational orders is not a
+truncation accident.  The displayed one-dimensional constant is the analytic
+expectation for fixed exact root data before the common-additive gauge; the
+wrapper does not infer a finite-system kernel dimension from the quotient
+remainder.
+
+### 7.3 Target-independent negative control
+
+For
+
+```text
+g=y^2-x^2-x,
+tau_+ = (x^2+x+c_2)^(1/2),    tau_-=-tau_+,
+```
+
+the coefficients of `x^-1=t^1` in `1/g_y(tau_+)` and
+`1/g_y(tau_-)` are `+1/2` and `-1/2`.  The failure is independent of the
+target, and the wrapper reports exactly `failure_order_t=1`.
+
+### 7.4 Vacuity mutation and saturation control
+
+For the passing cubic shear take `x=z^-3`, let
+`omega=(-1+sqrt(3)I)/2`, and index the exact roots as
+
+```text
+tau_j=-omega^(-j)z^-1,       j=0,1,2.
+```
+
+Mutate one **independent** tame slot at exponent `z^1`, carrying its conjugates
+with it:
+
+```text
+tau_j -> -omega^(-j)z^-1 + a omega^j z.
+```
+
+The wrapper checks all three identities
+`tau_j(omega z)=tau_(j+1)(z)`, so this repair avoids the invalid one-branch
+mutation.  Multiplying the three factors gives exactly
+
+```text
+product_j (y-tau_j)
+  = y^3 + 3a y + z^-3 - a^3 z^3
+  = y^3 + 3a y + x - a^3 t.
+```
+
+The first forbidden positive coefficient of the purported polynomial input
+`g-c_2` is therefore `-a^3` at `z^3=t^1`.  This is an input-polynomiality
+failure reported at an exact order; the system is rejected before target
+interpolation.  To prevent `a=0` from masquerading as a mutation, the wrapper
+declares
+
+```text
+ring:  QQ[a,sat_witness], lex(a,sat_witness)
+ideal: <a^3, sat_witness*a-1>.
+```
+
+Its Groebner basis is `[1]`, so no nonzero mutation passes that guard.  The
+leading separations, cubic degree leader, and `c=-1` are fixed nonzero units.
+This is `SATURATED-EMPTY` for the covariant input-mutation control only, not
+for a D=105 target or for a completed interpolation ideal.
+
+## 8. Reading the result
+
+### 8.1 Does the first global order overdetermine?
+
+For the **blind restricted count**, A is overdetermined at `k=12,14,16` and
+not at `k=18,20,22,24`; B is overdetermined by 9; C is overdetermined by 1.
+That faithfully reproduces the charged GPT-5.5 table.
+
+For the **exact global system**, the answer is `UNDECIDED` for A, B, and C.
+There is no known `Q_*`, no intrinsic `U(Q_*)`, and no instantiated
+`C(Q_*)`.  At a positive invariant order POLY may add 70 rows, while outer and
+shared variables may add columns.  Galois descent may remove repetitions and
+identify parameters.  One cannot select only whichever side helps a kill.
+
+C's `34`-versus-`35` razor is therefore a well-motivated experiment design,
+not a computed cokernel.  In the restricted 35-by-34 fiction, full column
+rank would leave a row cokernel of at least one.  The actual global matrix may
+have more or fewer intrinsic columns and dependent rows.
+
+### 8.2 What a rank dependency would mean
+
+A dependency means that a nominal coefficient condition does not cut a new
+tangent direction on the component being tested.  Possible sources include a
+universal root identity, a Galois repetition, a common-additive gauge,
+character cancellation, an ancestor-sharing identity, or a relation special
+to the star/outer coefficients.  For C, one exact dependency in a genuine
+35-by-34 descended matrix would remove the count razor and identify a
+structural compatibility to propagate to later orders.  It would not by
+itself prove existence or all-order survival.
+
+Conversely, a sampled ambient rank at arbitrary values of algebraically
+related star and root-of-unity parameters is not a rank on a solution
+component.  It cannot be promoted to a kill without the ring map and component
+check.
+
+### 8.3 What `SATURATED-EMPTY` would buy
+
+If, after enumerating every actual decoration/component of A, B, and C, each
+ideal saturated at the full nondegenerate product were empty, all three true
+`D=105` groups would be killed.  Since the rebased census identifies 105 as
+the smallest surviving degree above 100 and the next surviving degree is 108,
+the conclusion would be only
+
+```text
+D_min >= 108.
+```
+
+It would not prove a uniform degree theorem or the Jacobian conjecture.  This
+lane has no such emptiness result, so even that limited conclusion is not
+available here.
+
+## 9. Bounded OPENs
+
+1. `OPEN[D105-FULL-DECORATION]`.  Bounded quantity: for the nine charged
+   `(group,k)` choices, place and label exactly 105 roots, specify all pairwise
+   contacts through the first invariant order and the `D_2` guard, give the
+   cyclic permutation/covariance and sharing classes, and provide all needed
