+### 6.1 Why no saturated ideal was attempted
+
+A target saturation requires a declared coefficient field, polynomial ring,
+generator order, the ideal component, and the localization product containing
+all discriminants, unit leaders, `c`, and degree leaders.  The outer
+discriminants and leaders are among the missing decoration data, and there is
+no target ideal to extract.  Running `sat()` on a list of symbolic names would
+violate the campaign guardrail.  Therefore `EMPTY=NOT COMPUTED` on all target
+rows.
+
+No result is typed `RANK-EXCESS`: an ambient generic rank away from the target
+variety would not supply componentwise codimension.  No result is typed
+`SATURATED-EMPTY`: the localized ideal was not formed.  No result is typed
+`SURVIVES-TO-Q`: absence of a test is not passage through a test.
