+|---|---|---|
+| A | `(3,75,105)` | `(2,50,70)` |
+| B | `(3,90,105)` | `(2,60,70)` |
+| C | `(3,84,105)` | `(2,56,70)` |
+
+These give sizes along a distinguished chain.  As the framework stresses at
+lines 490-498, they do not give the full set partition of all leaves.
+
+### 3.1 Fixed star and normalization
+
+The reviewed normalized star is
+
+```text
+p_g(pi)=pi^3-pi,       p_f(pi)=pi^2-2/3.
+```
+
+It satisfies
+
+```text
+2 p_f p_g' - 3 p_g p_f' = 4/3 = kappa.
+```
+
+Because `kappa=cde/q`, retaining this exact normalization fixes the Jacobian
+constant rather than leaving it as `c=1`:
+
+| group | `q` | `c=kappa*q/(de)` |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| A | `1/2` | `1/9` |
+| B | `9/13` | `2/13` |
+| C | `9/17` | `2/17` |
+
+All are nonzero.  A run normalizing `c=1` would have to rescale `p_f`; it may
+not simultaneously claim the fixed star above unchanged.  In the target
+systems contemplated here `c` is specialized to the displayed nonzero
+constant, so it adds no intrinsic unknown.  A future unspecialized run must
+add one unknown and saturate at `c`.
+
+## 4. The maximum decoration justified by the inputs
+
+### 4.1 Partial rooted tree
+
+Each marked bottom star accounts for three `g`-leaves.  If, as a completion
+assumption, all marked stars are put inside the distinguished `D_2` cluster,
+the unresolved counts are:
+
+| group | `k` | marked `3k` | unmarked inside distinguished `D_2`: `a_2-3k` | outside that `D_2`: `105-a_2` |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| A | 12 | 36 | 39 | 30 |
+| A | 14 | 42 | 33 | 30 |
+| A | 16 | 48 | 27 | 30 |
+| A | 18 | 54 | 21 | 30 |
+| A | 20 | 60 | 15 | 30 |
+| A | 22 | 66 | 9 | 30 |
+| A | 24 | 72 | 3 | 30 |
+| B | 13 | 39 | 51 | 15 |
+| C | 17 | 51 | 33 | 21 |
+
+Even that containment is not route-to-tree data supplied by the census.  The
+table is an audit of how much remains to place, not a completed tree.
+
+### 4.2 Cover-polynomial action and a conditional series ansatz
+
+For every group the bottom denominator increment is `A_1=2` and
+`Q_1=3=1*2+1`.  Under the additional head/eigencharacter identification, the
+formal local-cover involution is `pi -> -pi`; the normalized star is compatible
+with it because its roots split as the fixed root `{0}` and the pair
+`{-1,+1}`.  This does not assert an attained physical-disc stabilizer: the
+required head and permutation data are absent.
+
+At level two the data are:
+
+| group | `A_2` | `Q_2=V_3 d_2/d_3=u` | division | selected `V_2=1` branch |
+|---|---:|---:|---|---|
+| A | 18 | 25 | `25=1*18+7` | (10), nonzero root |
+| B | 13 | 30 | `30=2*13+4` | (10), nonzero root |
+| C | 17 | 28 | `28=1*17+11` | (10), nonzero root |
+
+Moh's automorphism mechanism, transcribed and explained at
+`census-rebase-opus5-20260902.md:137-149`, says a selected nonzero factor of
+the relevant local cover polynomial `p(pi)` is accompanied by its full orbit
+of `A_2` distinct conjugate factors.  It does **not** say that these factors
+are `A_2` physical bottom discs or `A_2` branches of `g-c_2`.
+
+For bookkeeping only, one can make the following conditional ansatz.  Assume
+a route identifying a copy of each cover factor with a star-bearing series
+packet; let `zeta` be a primitive `R_delta`-th root, put
+`r_i=R_delta*delta_i`, choose `b!=0`, and write the shared ancestor prefix as
+`w_<delta2`.  Then a covariant formal copy would be
+
+```text
+tau_(j,c)(z)
+ = w_<delta2(zeta^j z)
+   + b zeta^(r_2 j) z^r_2
+   + c zeta^(r_1 j) z^r_1
+   + higher,
+
+j mod A_2,    c in {-1,0,+1}.
+```
+
+The three substitutions are:
+
+```text
+A: R=36, A_2=18, (r_2,r_1)=(14,21)
+B: R=26, A_2=13, (r_2,r_1)=(4,11)
+C: R=34, A_2=17, (r_2,r_1)=(8,19).
+```
+
+This is group-level cover bookkeeping, not a `k`-packet template; in
+particular, the `3A_2` displayed labels disagree with `3k` except in the three
+cardinality-matched cases.  If one further assumes
+`w_<delta2(zeta^A2 z)=w_<delta2(z)` and compatible `A_2`-step closure for every
+higher coefficient, then after `A_2` applications of `z -> zeta z` the formal
+centre returns and `zeta^(r_1 A_2)=-1`, so `c` changes to `-c`.  Only under
+those extra assumptions do the displayed leading labels cycle with sizes
+`A_2` for `c=0` and `2A_2` for the combined nonzero labels.  These are not
+promoted as leaf or disc orbits.  The missing route-to-tree theorem is exactly
+what would be needed to make that identification.
+
+If this ansatz is used as a synthetic model, later coefficients must transform
+by
+
+```text
+u_(j+1,c,r) = zeta^r u_(j,c,r),
+```
+
+with the wrap sending `c` to `-c`.  Giving every formal copy an independent
+tail, or merely giving conjugate tails the same symbol without the character
+factor, would not even realize this conditional action.
+
+### 4.3 UNI and the requested “coarsest split”
+
+The arithmetic identity `N=k V_2 q`, together with `kV_2<=u`, yields the nine
+formal choices in the charge.  It is a capacity/integrality computation, not
+an orbit construction or attainment theorem.  The requested `UNI` decoration
+adds the assumption “these `k` physical bottom discs form one orbit,” but the
+charged data contains neither the permutation nor its covariance on the 105
+root series.  Consequently **all nine UNI decorations remain open inputs**.
+The coincidences `k=A_2` in A/18, B/13, and C/17 are suggestive numerical
+compatibilities only; matching cardinalities do not give a map from cover
+factors to discs.
+
+There is no second, canonically “coarsest” several-orbit decoration in the
+charged data.  The maximal-free-orbit decomposition of the scalar level
+polynomial permits the numerical patterns
+
+```text
+A: 18 + residual fixed multiplicity 7
+B: 13 + 13 + residual fixed multiplicity 4
+C: 17 + residual fixed multiplicity 11.
+```
+
+The residual is multiplicity at the fixed zero of the scalar action, not that
+many distinct `V_2=1` bottom discs.  B's cover polynomial can contain two
+nonzero 13-orbits; after selecting only one such orbit it can instead be
+described as `13 + fixed-zero multiplicity 17`.  There is no licensed
+identification of either nonzero orbit with the selected `k=13` disc packet
+and no supplied major/minor or `q` data for a second physical packet.  Thus
+every requested `SPLIT` run is
+`OPEN[SPLIT-ORBIT-DATA]`; replacing it by singleton or “generic” disc orbits
+would be a new modelling convention.
+
+### 4.4 Every assumption and missing field
+
+The conditional formula above assumes a route from the selected nonzero cover
+factor to a star-bearing series packet, uses the least denominator of the
+three radii, fixes `b!=0`, fixes the star's affine/scalar normalization, and
+uses the formal cyclic action generated by `z -> zeta z`.  None of the route,
+the physical-disc interpretation, or the full action is derived.  It also does
+**not** assume that the remaining leaves are singletons or that unsupported
+tail coefficients vanish.
+
+A valid framework input still needs all of the following.
+
+1. A labelled rooted tree that places all `105-3k` residual leaves and records
+   every `D_2` incidence, with an ultrametric contact for every pair.  Only
+   under the optional single-distinguished-`D_2` containment assumption does
+   this specialize to `a_2-3k` leaves inside and `105-a_2` outside.
+2. The cyclic permutation and stabilizer on every residual leaf, plus an
+   explicit coefficient covariance check.  The bottom-disc label `UNI` does
+   not determine this permutation.
+3. Every centre coefficient in `w_<delta2`, every outer/minor leading
+   coefficient, and every tail coefficient capable of reaching the requested
+   moment order.
+4. The tame exponent semigroup.  The displayed `D_2` gap is a forced outer
+   activation; the charged review expressly warns that it need not be the
+   first exponent of each inner root tail.
+5. The equivalence/character relation for every shared coefficient at each
+   tree vertex.
+6. Nonzero separation leaders and discriminants for all strata, not only the
+   star discriminant.
+7. A finite last-supplied exponent sufficient to determine `D_i^-1` through
+   the residue and interpolation window.
+8. A value/definition for the adapter field `v`.  The D=105 census does not
+   print it; the sealed driver merely requires a nonnegative value.  Choosing
+   `v=0` would be an input adapter assumption, not a derived fact.
+9. If a condition on `g` alone rather than a fixed generic fibre is wanted,
+   target-independence over a transcendental `c_2`, modulo the one harmless
+   common additive constant.
+
+## 5. Exact system schema and order reached
+
+Once a complete separable 105-root packet of one polynomial `g-c_2` is
+supplied, its Galois covariance is verified, and the inverse guard is closed,
+the exact moment-form system is:
+
+```text
+D_i = product_(j != i) (tau_i-tau_j),       W_i=D_i^-1,
+[z^R] W_i = 0,                              NO-RESIDUE,
+q H_i[q] = -c R W_i[q+R]  (q != 0),         H_i[0]=a_orbit,
+M_r = sum_i H_i tau_i^r W_i.
+```
+
+At each retained exponent, the monic degree block is the 35-row family
+
+```text
+[z^q]M_r=0                 for r=0,...,33,
+[z^q]M_34 = 1 if q=0, and 0 otherwise.
+```
+
+At a forbidden positive invariant exponent, polynomiality adds the 70 rows
+
+```text
+[z^q]M_r=0                 for r=35,...,104,
+```
+
+which, after DEG and using that the elementary symmetric coefficients of the
+complete root packet lie in `C[x]`, is unit-triangularly equivalent to testing
+the remaining Lagrange coefficients after the already-counted monic identity.
+Thus “35 equations
+per order” is only the DEG block.  A positive invariant global order normally
+has 105 DEG-plus-POLY slots before dependencies; NO-RESIDUE contributes `h`
+once when its guard is reached.
+
+The first nonvacuous global exponent is
+
+```text
+Q_* = first exponent in the invariant support at which one of
+      M_0,...,M_34-target or a forbidden tail is nonzero as a polynomial.
+```
+
+It cannot be read from `delta_1-delta_2`.  The junction number is provenance
+for activation of outer factors, while `Q_*` is an actual exponent of a
+global orbit trace.  In the minimal uniformizers the junction indices
+`7,7,11` are not multiples of `R=36,26,34`; a nontrivial character can cancel
+at the trace before influencing a later invariant order.  The complete
+templates decide which products do so.
+
+Accordingly the target order actually reached in this lane is:
+
+```text
+arithmetic/tree provenance:  D_2 gap reached exactly;
+restricted homogeneous L_E: operator evaluated exactly at the D_2 gap;
+global DEG/POLY emission:     no order reached (Q_* undefined);
+global rank/saturation:       not started because no complete decoration was supplied.
+```
+
+This is an input stop, not a timeout.  The bounded wrapper runs in under five
+seconds and under 70 MB.
+
+### 5.1 Exact restricted `D_2` operator
+
+Write
+
+```text
+phi=u_0+u_1 pi+u_2 pi^2,      gamma=v_0+v_1 pi+v_2 pi^2+v_3 pi^3,
+lambda_f=-2mu,                lambda_g=-3mu.
+```
+
+Linearizing LOCAL-KELLER at a correction of relative order `E` gives
+
+```text
+L_E(phi,gamma)
+ =(lambda_f+E)phi p_g' + lambda_f p_f gamma'
+  -(lambda_g+E)gamma p_f' - lambda_g p_g phi'.
+```
+
+In columns `(u_0,u_1,u_2,v_0,v_1,v_2,v_3)` and rows
+`(pi^0,...,pi^4)`, its exact matrix is
+
+```text
+[ 2mu-E       0        0        0       4mu/3      0       0 ]
+[   0       -E-mu      0      6mu-2E      0       8mu/3    0 ]
+[ 3E-6mu      0      -E-4mu     0      4mu-2E      0      4mu]
+[   0       3E-3mu     0        0         0      2mu-2E    0 ]
+[   0         0       3E        0         0         0     -2E]
+```
+
+Substitution gives:
+
+| group | `mu` | `E=delta_1-delta_2` | `E/mu` | rank | kernel | row cokernel |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| A | `1/12` | `7/36` | `7/3` | 5 | 2 | 0 |
+| B | `3/26` | `7/26` | `7/3` | 5 | 2 | 0 |
+| C | `3/34` | `11/34` | `11/3` | 5 | 2 | 0 |
+
+For A and B a kernel basis is
+
+```text
+(0,2/3,0,-1/3,0,1,0),
+(4/15,0,2/3,0,1/15,0,1).
+```
+
+For C the first vector is the same and the second is
+
+```text
+(4/3,0,2/3,0,5/3,0,1).
+```
+
+These ranks and bases are exact rational SymPy computations.  They establish
+only the restricted local two-parameter fibre.  Outer factors enlarge the
+coefficient spaces and then impose sharing; the global moments couple every
+disc and every residual leaf.
+
